to in-range>?     top <= and{ >  }
to in-range><?    top <  and{ >  }


to clear-stacks   clear-data clear-control

~~ 2026-11-24 - GPT-6 coding agent under Jean Hugues Noel Robert.
~~ Language errors use the common actor-local VM exception boundary.
~~ Without a registered handler, vm-raise still fails explicitly through
~~ FATAL; it must not turn an unhandled exception into a success.
to FATAL-hook    vm-raise
to FATAL         /FATAL-hook tag.run
~~ An ordinary language-level raise may be recovered by the nearest catch.
~~ Keep FATAL's fail-fast fallback when no handler exists.
to raise         vm-raise

~~ Ordinary language lookup failures must respect the same exception and
~~ finally contract as explicit raise. The old clear-stacks handlers removed
~~ the caller's control frames, silently skipping on-return and corrupting
~~ nested method dispatch when called within an exception boundary.
to missing-verb     "missing-verb "     over join FATAL
to missing-method   "missing-method "   over join FATAL
to missing-operator "missing-operator " over join FATAL

~~ VM-resume continuations for the guard's normal/exceptional branches.
~~ The VM owns the control/data-stack cleanup and the block references.
to guard-success       guard-success-primitive
to guard-catch-finish  guard-catch-finish-primitive

to ASSERT-hook   "ASSERT" out debugger clear-stacks
to ASSERT        /ASSERT-hook tag.run
to assert{       assert. inline

to constant:is:  make.constant
to global:is:    make.global

to void-constant  _ swap, make.constant
to void-global    _ swap, make.global
to void-local     _ swap, make.local

to init-globals
  constant: inox-version/       is: "v0.4.0";
  constant: inox-version-time/  is: 1674589501; ~~ ToDo: overflow when ms
  constant: true/               is: 1 ? :true;
  constant: false/              is: 0   :false;
  constant: on/                 is: 1 ? :on;
  constant: off/                is: 0 ? :off;
  constant: yes/                is: 1 ? :yes;
  constant: no/                 is: 0 ? :no;
  constant: failure/            is: 0 ? :failure;
  constant: success/            is: 1 ? :success;
  constant: with/               is: with/ :with;
  global:   safe/               is: "safe";
init-globals


