to it++            it top ++ it!
to it{             run-with-it
to do-with-it      run-with-it


to times:do:
  it{
    it >runable, it!
    if: it >0 then: {
      while: { it-- >0 } do: {
        runable> .run()
      };
    };
  }

to times:loop:  times:do:.
to times        swap times:do:.


to it-self       it >self
to self          self>
to this-it       it >this
to this          this>
to that-it       it >that
to that          that>

to ii            it.  inline
to ii!           it!. inline
to upper         upper-local
to upper!        upper-local!
to jj            /it 1 upper
to jj!           /it 1 upper!
to kk            /it 2 upper
to kk!           /it 2 upper!
to ll            /it 3 upper
to ll!           /it 3 upper!

~~ 2026-11-22: GPT-6 coding agent, under Jean Hugues Noel Robert.
~~ Postfix comparisons are explicit; the original mixed form combined with
~~ loop-while's broken checker stopped early. Use the fixed iterative VM.
to from:to:do:
  it{
    it >runable, >ii-to, ii!
    if: ii ii-to> <= then: {
      do: { runable> .run() } while: { ++it ii-to> <= };
    };
  }

to from:down-to:do:
  it{
    it >runable, >ii-down-to, ii!
    if: ii ii-down-to> >= then: {
      do: { runable> .run() } while: { --it ii-down-to> >= };
    };
  }

~~ 2026-11-22: GPT-6 coding agent, under Jean Hugues Noel Robert.
~~ The step direction and range comparisons must use proper postfix operands;
~~ rely on the repaired loop-while primitive instead of recursion.
to from:to:by:do:
  it{
    it >runable, >ii-by, >ii-to, ii!
    if: ii-by> 0 > then: {
      if: ii ii-to> <= then: {
        do: { runable> .run() } while: { ii ii-by> + ii! ii ii-to> <= };
      };
    } else: {
      if: ii-by> 0 < then: {
        if: ii ii-to> >= then: {
          do: { runable> .run() } while: { ii ii-by> + ii! ii ii-to> >= };
        };
      } else: {
        "from:to:by:do: zero step" FATAL
      };
    };
  }


