~~ 2026-11-24: GPT-6 coding agent under Jean Hugues Noel Robert.
~~ Complete the 2023 try-run and try/catch/finally family in Inox itself.
~~ The VM provides only the general actor-local exception boundary and
~~ nonlocal scope unwind. Without catch, try-run has no guard overhead.
~~ `scope` creates the control-stack scope for the on-return continuation.
~~ Important FBF: `with` is a formal-parameter marker and is NOT a scope;
~~ using it here left one unwanted data-stack tag per call.
~~ Finalizers run on normal and exceptional exits, including errors raised
~~ by a catch handler. The cleanup block is run exactly once.
to try-run  .run. inline
to try      try-run. inline

to try:catch: run-guarded. inline

to try:finally: >cleanup-block >try-block
  { scope
      $cleanup-block on-return
      $try-block .run
  } .run. inline

to try:catch:finally: >cleanup-block >catch-block >try-block
  { scope
      $cleanup-block on-return
      $try-block $catch-block run-guarded
  } .run. inline


